 "extraction": "VizieR ASU TSV export, -out=**&-out.max=unlimited. Cleaned file maps upstream columns to a standard schema (id,ra_deg,dec_deg,z,z_err,q_flag,member_flag) and appends sep_arcmin and R_proj_Mpc computed from the cluster centre with FlatLambdaCDM(H0=70,Om0=0.3). No rows dropped. Where the upstream redshift is stored as a velocity cz in km/s it is converted to z=cz/c and its uncertainty is converted consistently to dz=e_cz/c; otherwise no values are altered. Raw upstream response kept verbatim in raw/.",
 "note": "Abell 2029 (z=0.0773). Sohn, Geller, Zahid & Fabricant 2019, ApJ 872, 192 ('Physical properties of the spectroscopic members of A2029'). 1215 rows, ALL spectroscopic cluster MEMBERS (members-only table), giving the largest member sample for A2029 in this product. Instrument: MMT/Hectospec plus SDSS. Selection function: magnitude-limited r-band, no colour cut. Sky coverage: members extend to ~96 arcmin (~8.7 Mpc projected, i.e. well into the infall region); 90% within ~4.2 Mpc - the widest radial baseline of any catalogue here. Carries log stellar mass and other derived properties. Substantially overlaps Sohn+2017 and Sohn+2019 (ApJ 871,129); do not stack these three without de-duplicating on sky position.",
